  "system": {
    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide\">Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide</a></i> </p><p>The Lanvarok is an ancient weapon that comes in two varieties: the&nbsp;Sith Lanvarok, and the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Massassi_Lanvarok\" title=\"Massassi Lanvarok\">Massassi Lanvarok</a>. The Sith Lanvarok is a wrist-mounted weapon that fires small discs at the target, dealing damage comparable to a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Blaster_Pistol\" title=\"Blaster Pistol\">Blaster Pistol</a>. </p><p>A Sith Lanvarok is worn, not held, freeing up the wielder's hands for melee weapons. A Sith Lanvarok is treated as a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Pistol\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pistol\">Pistol</a> for the purpose of determining <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Range\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Range\">Range</a>, and a wielder can fire a Sith Lanvarok as though it were a second weapon for the purpose of <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Two-Weapon_Fighting\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Two-Weapon Fighting\">Two-Weapon Fighting</a>. </p><p>A Sith Lanvarok requires disc ammunition, and can hold up to 5 discs at a time; after 5 shots, the discs must be replaced. Each disc weighs 0.1 kg and costs 5 credits. </p><p><b>Inaccurate:</b>&nbsp;This weapon cannot fire at targets at Long <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Range\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Range\">Range</a>. </p>",
